WEBVTT

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.530
Remember this.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.500
I shall become your soeur, without fail.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.700
What are you doing, Yumi?

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.480
You're going to be late if you
don't hurry up and eat breakfast.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.040
Yuki! Knock before you come in!

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.420
Again?

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:31.660
What have you been sighing about all morning?

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:35.130
Say, for the school festival,

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.220
we're inviting the Hanadera Student
Body President and putting on a play,

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.130
but what kind of person is
the Student Body President?

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.840
What kind of person is he?

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.800
He makes me sort of nervous.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.870
He's cool, he gets good grades,
and his family is impressive... I guess?

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.910
That sounds like Sachiko-sama.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.190
The maidens, who flock to
Maria-sama's garden,

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:09.060
pass through the tall gates today yet
again with innocent, angelic smiles.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:13.900
Their pure hearts and bodies are
clad in deep-colored uniforms.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.310
So that the pleats of their
skirts are not disturbed...

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.370
...and so that their white sailor
collars are not set aflutter,

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.870
it is customary here to walk
slowly and with decorum.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:28.880
The Private Lillian Girls' Academy,
a garden of maidens.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:42.160
Maria Watches Over Us

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.940
An Unnerving Duet

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.410
Good morning, Yumi-san.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:14.550
Rosa Chinensis!

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.380
And... Sachiko-sama...

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:18.420
Good morning.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:20.890
G-Good morning!

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.460
Let us go, Onee-sama.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.240
The Red Rose soeurs certainly are quite elegant.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:35.730
Onee-sama,

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.410
do you suppose it's true that
there's a first year student...

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:39.470
...who rejected Sachiko-sama?

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.740
As members of the school paper,

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.540
we'll want a detailed account of the truth on this.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.250
Yes, Onee-sama.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:50.760
Rumors spread quickly.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.430
And by noon the next day,

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:57.700
all the students in the high school division...

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:58.430
Year 1, Peach Class
all the students in the high school division...

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.600
Year 1, Peach Class
...knew that I had rejected Sachiko-sama.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.070
Hey, hey, is she here?!

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.100
Where? Where?

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.500
Which one is Fukuzawa Yumi-san?

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.000
Tsutako-san, did you tell someone?

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:12.470
Certainly not!

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:16.520
These things are far more enjoyable
to watch than to participate in.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.860
But if you need to be told who started the rumor,

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.550
that's both a fortunate and
unfortunate thing for you.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.180
I have such mixed feelings about this.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.060
It might be better not to be in the
classroom during lunch breaks.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:34.070
After all, I heard through the
grapevine that the school paper...

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:35.470
...is coming to cover the story.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.940
And they have a bunch of people as good as...

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.300
...any entertainment reporter out there.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.330
Please excuse me.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:42.570
See? Here they come.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:46.380
If I released that photo,
I bet the response would be huge.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:47.980
Hold on, Tsutako-san!

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.520
Shimako-san...

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.710
Yumi-san, this way.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.320
Do you always have lunch way out here?

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.430
It's a seasonal thing.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.790
Nice days during the spring and autumn.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.300
What about summer?

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.670
This cherry blossom tree becomes
infested with hairy caterpillars,

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.930
so I don't really like that.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.810
But in a short while, a lot of gingko
nuts will come falling down,

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.210
so I'm looking forward to that.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.440
You're strange, Shimako-san.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:21.810
Am I?

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.850
But as long as the gingko nuts don't
get reduced to a pulp underfoot,

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:26.480
they don't smell that much.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:30.050
So streets lined with gingko trees
where everyone walks are just tragic.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:35.230
Shimako-san, could it be that you take
those uncrushed gingko nuts home?

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:36.390
Bingo.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:40.460
Gingko nuts, lily bulbs, soybeans...
I love things like that.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:41.560
I thought so.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.230
You're interesting, Shimako-san.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.700
You are too, Yumi-san.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.310
What?

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.670
I'm glad to have gotten to know you.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.420
Shimako-san, could I ask you something?

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:56.550
What is it?

00:05:56.550 --> 00:06:00.320
Why did you refuse Sachiko-sama's offer?

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.420
I thought that I would not
work out for Sachiko-sama.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:08.320
Likewise, Sachiko-sama would not
have worked out for me, either.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.260
In what way?

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:15.960
I like Sachiko-sama, but what we
seek from each other is different.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.900
So what we can give each other is different, too.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.900
It's too complicated for me to understand.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.440
Sachiko-sama said the same to me, too.

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.810
That she could understand
what I was trying to say,

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.210
but that I wasn't being specific.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:30.490
You know,

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:33.620
I think the shock of being refused by
you was greater for Sachiko-sama...

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.650
...than when I turned her down.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:37.950
It didn't look that way to me.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.050
That's because she's a contrary
person who hates to lose.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.530
When she's truly vexed, she acts prim.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:49.560
Why did you say that you couldn't be her soeur?

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:54.470
Shall we get going soon?

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.110
Be careful not to step on the gingko nuts.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:01.940
It could be...

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:02.510
What?

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:06.490
...that you and Sachiko-sama
would be a good match.

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:14.530
Let's call it a day soon.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:16.660
Yumi-san?

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:18.100
What?

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:21.540
Oh, I still haven't finished
writing the cleaning log,

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.630
so please go on without me.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.530
Then we'll take you up on your offer.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:25.840
Goodbye.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:26.570
See you tomorrow.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:27.630
Goodbye.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.270
I'll leave after everyone else has left.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:36.280
I don't want people staring at me.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.700
That was at the first-year
student welcome ceremony...

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.790
...hosted by the Yamayuri Council.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.010
What a shriek to let loose.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:53.130
You make it seem as though I were attacking you.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:58.860
I-If you approach silently from behind,
anyone would scream, Sachiko-sama!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:02.700
Play.

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:03.670
What?

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:04.700
One more time.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:05.760
Uh, um...

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:09.780
One, two, three, go.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:22.780
Wow, I'm playing a duet with Sachiko-sama!

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.560
I just can't do it, after all.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.520
I can't keep up with you, Sachiko-sama.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.720
Really? You were playing most splendidly.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:05.460
Shall we go soon?

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:06.730
What?

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:09.600
From now until the school festival,

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:12.700
you're going to attend the
Cinderella rehearsals with me.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:13.840
What?

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:18.400
After all, you're my understudy
for the role of Cinderella.

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.870
It would only be natural for you to rehearse.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:24.250
But isn't that only if I accept the rosary?

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:27.760
Are you so firmly convinced
that you won't accept it,

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.750
that you don't intend to attend rehearsals?

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.720
No, that's not...

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:34.660
I am going to attend them.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:38.360
Even though I'm confident
that I will make you my soeur.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:41.340
Since there are not many things in this world...

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.700
...that one can say are absolute.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:47.770
And it's preferable to disgracing
myself during the real performance.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:52.910
Certainly...

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:57.610
You must have your own thoughts
on the matter, so I won't force you.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:01.120
But won't you come watch me rehearse?

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:03.320
I will.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:07.520
Was that photograph taken yesterday morning?

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:11.760
I just remembered now.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:16.530
So when you saw the photograph,

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:19.370
you really didn't remember.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.470
Not as far as when it was.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:26.380
Then, I really met you for the
first time yesterday, didn't I?

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:27.310
Yes.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:29.950
I feel better now that I remember.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.720
Do you fix so many underclassmen's scarves...

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:36.280
...that you have trouble remembering?

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:40.490
I rarely... No, I almost never do things like that.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.460
I wonder why I decided to do that?

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.830
I'm not a morning person
and my mind was in a fog,

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.430
so perhaps I stopped you without realizing it.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:53.230
That must be why I was unable
to remember it right away.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:56.270
Oh, my...

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:57.770
Yamamura-sensei.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:58.880
Good afternoon.

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:00.370
Good afternoon.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:03.480
I had thought it was some kind of mistake,

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:05.550
but was that rumor true?

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:06.480
What?

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:08.150
But how strange.

00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:11.480
Fukuzawa-san turned you down,
didn't she, Ogasawara-san?

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:13.750
So why are you two together?

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.420
Or is the truth that you said okay to her?

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:18.120
Um, so that was...

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:21.160
I am so sorry to have troubled you.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:24.670
We shall leave the matter of our
relationship to your imagination.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.730
Please excuse us now.

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:29.300
C-Certainly.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:33.040
You needn't say anything unnecessary.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.650
Rumors have a way of
growing more outlandish...

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:38.170
...the more we respond to them.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.060
If there's something that requires an explanation,

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.460
don't parcel it out in bits and pieces.

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:44.990
Rather, when those around
you are prepared to listen,

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:46.690
explain it clearly just once.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:49.560
While they are fussing about it,
let it go like wind through willows.

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:50.360
I understand.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:52.560
But...

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:57.170
I think silencing a teacher with
a smile like Sachiko-sama did...

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:01.140
...is a feat that no ordinary high
school student can accomplish.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:07.210
Maria Watches Over Us

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:14.480
Oh, here's Sachiko.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:15.990
You're late!

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:22.550
I'm sorry for interrupting the rehearsal.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.170
Now, please continue.

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:43.540
Wow, Sachiko-sama and
Rei-sama dancing together!

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.080
Yumi-chan.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.250
Come over here.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:49.360
Rosa Chinensis...

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:53.750
Not bad, are they?

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.020
For having been matched
up for the first time today.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.190
The first time?!

00:13:57.670 --> 00:14:00.070
We learn the rudiments of dance in class...

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:04.470
...and Sachiko is an honest-to-goodness
young lady of a wealthy family,

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:08.310
so it's only natural that she
knows the social dances.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:10.500
I had no idea.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.180
It seems Rei used her ability to focus
from her martial arts training...

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:16.340
...to memorize the dance,

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.480
but she still has some difficulties.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:20.780
See?

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:26.660
Sachiko has been studying
ballet since she was five, too.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:27.930
English conversation, piano,

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.300
tea ceremonies and flower arrangement...

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.230
She's generally knowledgeable
in all those things.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.330
Up through middle school,

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:36.930
it seems she had some tutor
or other coming every day.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.460
Wow, it's like a different world.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:41.770
Right?

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.570
It's so stifling.

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:46.580
That's why I made her quit it all.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:50.110
Or perhaps I should say,
I made it so she was forced to quit.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:51.820
Because I made her my soeur...

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.520
...and dragged her into doing all
sorts of Yamayuri Council chores.

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:59.430
You see, Sachiko is an earnest person at heart,

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:02.230
so when she's faced with expectations,
she does exactly that.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:05.060
That's why she needs to take
a break once in a while.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.470
Do you understand that?

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:08.130
Sort of...

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:09.670
That's fine.

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:17.140
But if she's used to dancing often,

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.450
it doesn't seem like she
should be unwilling now,

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:20.970
just because her partner will be a boy...

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:24.310
That was actually the
question on our minds, too.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:27.050
To Sachiko, it's just a dance.

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:30.050
So why would she refuse to do it?

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.790
She was so adamantly against it,

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:33.990
we wanted to know the reason behind it...

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:36.720
...and that was why we didn't allow
her to step down right away, but...

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:39.930
Things have become even more
interesting, haven't they?

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:44.700
With the addition of a spice
called Fukuzawa Yumi.

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:48.940
It's just as Rosa Gigantea said.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:49.970
What?

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:53.980
When you become lost in thought,
you tend to make funny faces.

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:55.470
No, um...

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:01.210
Sachiko, about your starting position...

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:05.630
Stand a little more to stage left
and turn your attention this way.

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:07.420
Just what you'd expect of Rosa Chinensis.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.330
She's really paying attention to what's important.

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.230
Yumi-chan, can you dance?

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:16.340
No, not at all!

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:17.400
Oh?

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:21.700
Rosa Foetida, do we only have dance
classes starting in the second year?

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:23.940
I think so.

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:26.380
Then I'll teach you.

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.150
Huh?

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:27.940
Come on.

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:28.570
Oh...

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:33.120
Yumi-chan, you say a lot of,
"Huh?" and " Oh..." and " What?"

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:35.890
Rosa Gigantea!

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:38.890
This is a waltz, so it's triple time.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:42.120
One, two, three. One, two, three.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:45.360
One, two, three. One, two, three.

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:47.530
You're being too hesitant. Don't look down.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:51.400
One, two, three. One, two, three.

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:53.400
I don't care if you step on my feet.

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:55.110
Oh, whoops.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:17:00.210
I wonder if there'll be rumors
of you two-timing now.

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:06.180
Okay, I'm going to introduce
a new friend to all of you!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.590
This is Fukuzawa Yumi-chan!

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:11.360
She'll be participating in the
group dance starting today,

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:12.880
so please be nice to her!

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:14.020
Wha...

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.260
It's no fun just observing, right?

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:20.330
Besides, when you consider
the worst case scenario,

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.360
it'll be better if you're used to dancing.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:28.870
I thought you were betting that
Sachiko-sama would not win me over...

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:31.810
Someone partner up with her!

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:45.690
Then, I will.

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:48.920
B-But, you are dancing with Sachiko-sama...

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.250
I'm an understudy, after all.

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:54.940
When the actual person playing the
Prince comes from Hanadera,

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:55.900
I'll be stepping aside anyway.

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:59.540
So there won't be any problem
with me partnering up with you.

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:01.300
Come on.

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:14.880
I-I'm sorry!

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:16.420
It's okay.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:25.290
Sorry.

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:26.990
I'm fine.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:45.920
Pay attention.

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:50.450
You seem quite interested in Sachiko.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.620
No, it isn't like that.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:55.590
It's just that she's so utterly different from me...

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:06.000
Um, I forgot something, so please excuse me!

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:07.760
Oh, Yumi-chan!

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:21.090
Yumi-san?

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:22.910
Katsura-san...

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.230
Um, what's going on?

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:26.630
W-With what?

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:29.690
Someone from the Dance Club
was talking earlier...

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:31.700
...that you're going to be appearing...

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:33.930
...in the play produced by
the Yamayuri Council officers.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.070
If you call it "appearing."

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:39.940
I'm just going to be dancing in the background.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:43.740
But they said your partner was
to be Rosa Foetida en bouton.

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.870
Yes, well...

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:47.450
It's true?

00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:49.670
Yumi-san, good afternoon!

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.150
Good afternoon!

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:52.740
G-Good afternoon...

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:56.690
As it so happens, we were
just talking about you, Yumi-san.

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:57.950
I-I see.

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:00.920
Could we take this opportunity
to ask you for a clear answer?

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:04.700
Is it true that you turned
down Sachiko-sama's offer?

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:07.600
If so, why have you been seen
in each other's company?

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:13.470
What role are you playing within
the Yamayuri Council group?

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:16.500
Which of the dear sisters do you like best?

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:19.640
At a time like this, if it were Sachiko-sama...

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:26.010
Everyone, I'm sorry to have troubled you.

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.220
D-Due to circumstances,

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:31.780
I am going to be helping with the
Yamayuri Council officers' play.

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:36.320
That is the reason why the officers
have been approaching me.

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.760
Then, what about the matter
concerning Sachiko-sama?

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:40.160
Sachiko-sama?

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:44.290
Is it true that Sachiko-sama
asked you to be her soeur?

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:47.400
The word is that you turned her down, though.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:50.740
At a time like this, if it were Sachiko-sama...

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:53.670
That's just a rumor, right?

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:57.410
Right, Yumi-san?

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:00.450
If it were Sachiko-sama...

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:05.180
I shall leave the matter to your...

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:08.050
Sachiko-sama would...

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.820
Sachiko-sama would...

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:14.630
...never seriously choose
someone like me to be her soeur!

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:16.300
Yumi-san?!

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:18.930
My, what are we to do?

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:20.310
We're sorry.

00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:23.330
We didn't ask you intending to making you cry.

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:28.540
Because I like her...

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:31.340
Because I like Sachiko-sama...

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:36.250
Because it would be too sad to have
just been the closest person around...

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:40.860
Why can't Sachiko-sama understand that?!

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:46.020
I was happier watching her from afar.

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:47.690
That way...

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:51.130
...I wouldn't have had to act
contrary to my own feelings.

00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:22.400
Preview

00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:22.960
Preview
Boohoohoo...

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:23.600
Preview
If you are going to weep about it,
Boohoohoo...

00:23:23.600 --> 00:23:24.000
Preview
If you are going to weep about it,

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.570
Preview
hurry up and accept the rosary!

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:26.030
Preview
Sachiko-sama might be perfect...

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:26.930
Sachiko-sama might be perfect...

00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:28.870
...for the role of Cinderella's mean step-sister.

00:23:28.870 --> 00:23:29.200
Quit grumbling!
...for the role of Cinderella's mean step-sister.

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:30.000
Quit grumbling!

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.810
I said it once I'll say it again! Become my soeur!

00:23:31.810 --> 00:23:32.340
To think such dialogue suits her so well...

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:33.140
Next Time
To think such dialogue suits her so well...
"The Moon and the Rosary"

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.140
Next Time
Sachiko-sama is pretty scary!
"The Moon and the Rosary"

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:36.610
Next Time
